Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:08.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Most agents don't have a tool problem. They have a context problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.00,0:00:19.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Before a task even begins, an agent can load dozens of tool schemas it may never use. Forty tools, twelve thousand four hundred estimated context tokens, for a task that only needs a few.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.00,0:00:29.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Toolpath takes a different approach. It models tools, capabilities, and entities as a graph, then resolves the path a task actually needs. Traverse, don't preload.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.00,0:00:41.00,Default,,0,0,0,,A task maps to capabilities. Graph traversal identifies the matching tools. Only those tools need to enter context. Three capabilities, three tools, one graph traversal, six hops.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.00,0:01:04.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's run the demo. The baseline preloads forty tools and estimates twelve thousand four hundred context tokens. Toolpath identifies three relevant tools: repository resolution, pull request reading, and issue creation. The graph makes that selection inspectable, and the execution log shows how the task progresses.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.00,0:01:16.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The result: one thousand eight hundred estimated context tokens instead of twelve thousand four hundred. An estimated reduction of around eighty-five percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.00,0:01:24.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The deployed demonstration uses a recorded snapshot, and the token figures are reproducible estimates, not live tokenizer measurements. Less unnecessary context. More deliberate tool selection.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.00,0:01:30.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Toolpath. Traverse, don't preload.
